date - print the date and time

SYNOPSIS
    date [+FORMAT]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the current date and time. With an argument beginning +, uses it
    as a strftime format.

    The clock is read from the CMOS at boot and advanced by the timer since,
    so it is right if the machine's battery-backed clock was. There is no
    timezone database: everything is UTC unless /etc/timezone holds an offset
    in minutes.

SEE ALSO
    uptime, touch
